## Scenarios

### JWT claim JSON encoding (json_encode_object)

#### quotes text values

- Verify: quotes text values


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 4 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: quotes text values")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val out = json_encode_object([("sub", "user123")])
assert_equal(out, "{\"sub\":\"user123\"}")
```

</details>

#### leaves integer values unquoted, including negatives

- Verify: leaves integer values unquoted, including negatives


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 4 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: leaves integer values unquoted, including negatives")
val out = json_encode_object([("exp", 1735689600), ("neg", -7)])
assert_equal(out, "{\"exp\":1735689600,\"neg\":-7}")
```

</details>

#### emits booleans unquoted as true/false, not digit-sniffed text

- Verify: emits booleans unquoted as true/false, not digit-sniffed text


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 4 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: emits booleans unquoted as true/false, not digit-sniffed text")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val out = json_encode_object([("admin", true), ("banned", false)])
assert_equal(out, "{\"admin\":true,\"banned\":false}")
```

</details>

#### handles a mixed claim set (text, int, bool together)

- Verify: handles a mixed claim set (text, int, bool together)


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 8 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: handles a mixed claim set (text, int, bool together)")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val out = json_encode_object([
    ("sub", "user123"),
    ("exp", 1735689600),
    ("admin", true),
])
assert_equal(out, "{\"sub\":\"user123\",\"exp\":1735689600,\"admin\":true}")
```

</details>

#### json_encode is a pass-through alias to json_encode_object

- Verify: json_encode is a pass-through alias to json_encode_object


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 4 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: json_encode is a pass-through alias to json_encode_object")
val tuples = [("k", "v")]
assert_equal(json_encode(tuples), json_encode_object(tuples))
```

</details>

